---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base 
  title="About Celestrium" 
  description="Celestrium is open research software for astronomical data access, analysis prototypes, and reproducible computational workflows."
  activeNav="about"
>
  <div class="about-page-header">
    <span class="ansi-tag">[PROJECT:ABOUT]</span>
    <span class="ansi-tag">SUB-SURFACE / ASTRO-THEORY</span>
    <h1 class="page-title">About Celestrium</h1>
    <p class="page-desc">
      Celestrium is an open software workbench for astronomical data access, analysis prototypes, and computational research workflows. Its research claims are under evidence review; this project page describes software scope, not validated scientific outcomes.
    </p>
    <div class="incomplete-rule"></div>
  </div>

  <section class="about-section">
    <div class="section-kicker">// CORE PHILOSOPHY</div>
    <h2 class="section-title">Research and engineering principles</h2>
    <p class="about-p">
      The repository combines archive clients, analysis code, model prototypes, and a CLI. The scientific validity of each workflow depends on its data provenance, assumptions, evaluation design, and reproducible outputs.
    </p>
    <p class="about-p">
      The following are development goals, not guarantees that every module currently meets them. Consult the implementation and its validation record before relying on any model output.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="standards-grid">
    <div class="standard-card">
      <div class="std-num">[STD 01]</div>
      <h3 class="std-title">Zero Naked Predictions</h3>
      <p class="std-desc">
        Report uncertainty appropriate to the model and estimand. A Dirichlet standard deviation is not, by itself, evidence of calibration; interval construction and empirical coverage must be checked on independent data.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="standard-card">
      <div class="std-num">[STD 02]</div>
      <h3 class="std-title">Disentangled RLCD Optimization</h3>
      <p class="std-desc">
        When comparing calibration strategies, state which parameters are frozen, which data fit the readout, and whether the loss is proper for the target. Report results on an untouched evaluation set.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="standard-card">
      <div class="std-num">[STD 03]</div>
      <h3 class="std-title">Stanford Debiased Error (NeurIPS 2019)</h3>
      <p class="std-desc">
        Calibration metrics depend on binning and sample size. Report bin counts and uncertainty intervals; distinguish a signed debiased estimator from its nonnegative display transform.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="standard-card">
      <div class="std-num">[STD 04]</div>
      <h3 class="std-title">Conformal Risk Control</h3>
      <p class="std-desc">
        Risk-control guarantees depend on the loss, calibration procedure, sampling assumptions, and threshold-selection method. Do not claim a bound until those assumptions and an independent evaluation have been documented.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="incomplete-rule"></div>

  <section class="about-section">
    <div class="section-kicker">// INFRASTRUCTURE & ECONOMICS</div>
    <h2 class="section-title">Hardware Architecture & Cloud Economics</h2>
    <p class="about-p">
      The repository supports local development and optional cloud experiments. Previously reported hardware and throughput figures are historical benchmark claims under audit, not service-level guarantees:
    </p>
    <ul class="about-list">
      <li><strong>Local development:</strong> Python and pytest workflows are available; run the tests in the supported environment before relying on a change.</li>
      <li><strong>Optional cloud compute:</strong> Modal integration code exists. Cloud availability, cost, and performance depend on the specific workload and environment.</li>
      <li><strong>Data handling:</strong> Some catalog paths use memory mapping and streaming. Memory use and throughput must be measured for each data source and configuration.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <div class="incomplete-rule"></div>

  <section class="about-section">
    <div class="section-kicker">// COLLABORATION MODEL</div>
    <h2 class="section-title">Autonomous Multi-Agent Pairing</h2>
    <p class="about-p">
      Celestrium is developed collaboratively. Experiments and manuscripts are version-controlled, but reproducibility varies by workflow; the release roadmap specifies the artifacts expected for public findings.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .about-page-header {
    max-width: var(--content-width);
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .page-title {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 2.3rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin: 1rem 0 1.2rem;
  }

  .page-desc {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  .about-section {
    margin: 3rem 0;
    max-width: var(--content-width);
  }

  .section-kicker {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-text-tertiary);
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }

  .section-title {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.8rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
  }

  .about-p {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
  }

  .standards-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 1.8rem;
    margin: 2.5rem 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .standards-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  .standard-card {
    background: var(--color-bg-subtle);
    padding: 1.8rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.8rem;
  }

  .std-num {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text-tertiary);
  }

  .std-title {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .std-desc {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  .about-list {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .about-list li {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  .about-list li strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
</style>
